Rule meanings:
- CP_EOL: control plane is past end of life
- CP_EOL_SOON: control plane reaches end of support soon
- CP_PATCH_BEHIND: control plane is several patches behind the latest patch
- CP_UNKNOWN_VERSION: control plane version is not in the supported-version matrix
- CP_UNSUPPORTED: control plane is past end of standard support (extended support)
- NODE_EOL: node pool runs a minor version past end of life
- NODE_NEWER_THAN_CP: node pool is newer than the control plane
- NODE_POOL_MIXED: node pool runs mixed minor versions (upgrade in progress or stuck)
- NODE_SKEW_EXCEEDED: node pool is too many minor versions behind the control plane
- UNPARSEABLE_VERSION: a reported version could not be parsed
- UNREACHABLE: cluster could not be checked

